A||N||13||Haze_Performance||1984 - 1988 Fiero Production Info||||7||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||09-16-2001||07:30 PM||||I received an email from a forum member that wanted Fiero production info. "Your email address wouldn't work so here ya go"<P><B>How many Fieros were made?</B> <BR>Breakdown by body style.<BR>1984: 7099 coupes + 62070 sport coupes + 66121 SEs + 2000 (May be 1500) Indy Pace Cars = 137340 <BR>1985: 5280 coupes + 23823 sport coupes + 24734 SEs + 22534 GTs = 76371 <BR>1986: 9143 coupes + 24866 sport coupes + 32305 SEs + 17660 GTs = 83974 <BR>1987: 23603 coupes + 3135 sport coupes + 3875 SEs + 15968 GTs = 46581 <BR>1988: 13910 coupes + 5643 Formulas + 6849 GTs = 26402 <P><B>Breakdown by color</B><BR> <BR>BR=Bright Red; BK=Black; W=White; S=Silver; RR=Ruby Red (Med. Red Met.); <BR>G=Light Gold Met; BB=Bright Blue; Y=Yellow<P>1984: 65684 BR, 27368 BK, 34211 W, 9579 S<P>1985: 24439 BR, 20620 BK, 12983 W, 18329 S<P>1986: 28563 BR, 21216 BK, 5228 W, 12637 S, 16325 G<P>1987: 2 BR, 8402 BK, 2611 W, 6671 S, 20264 RR, 4119 G, 4458 BB<P>1988: 10238 BR, 4602 BK, 6404 W, 1256 S, 2729 RR, 1166 Y<P><B>Breakdown by option</B><P><BR>Engine, 4-cylinder: 84=100% 85=55.0% 86=45.3% 87=60.5% 88=54.3%<P>Engine, V-6: 84=0.0% 85=45.0% 86=54.7%87=39.5% 88=45.7%<P>Transmission, 4-speed: 84=56.7% 85=21.8% 86=21.3% 87=0.0% 88=0.0%<P>Transmission, 5-speed: 84=0.0% 85=31.2% 86=28.6% 87=45.4% 88=52.4%<P>Transmission, Auto: 84=43.3% 85=47.0% 86=50.1% 87=54.6% 88=47.6%<P>Wheels. alloy: 84=78.0% 85=85.0% 86=69.8% 87=62.1% 88-99.9%<P>Air Conditioning: 84=79.3% 85=82.7% 86=89.3% 87=93.2% 88=89.3%<P>Tinted Glass: 84=94.1% 85=97.5% 86=75.5% 87=61.8% 88=71.9%<P>Windows, power: 84=45.3% 85=62.5% 86=42.0% 87=7.0% 88=13.3% (std on GT)<P>Door locks, power: 84=30.4% 85=41.6% 86=43.3% 87=36.9% 88=33.2%<P>Tilt column: 84=87.6% 85=96.2% 86=74.7% 87=60.5% 88=70.6%<P>Cruise Control: 84=40.3% 85=53.2% 86=52.4% 87=40.6% 88=49.6%<P>Sunroof: 84=50.2% 85=61.3% 86=61.4% 87=35.8% 88=36.6%<P>AM/FM stereo radio: 84=31.8% 85=32.3% 86=22.8% 87=36.8% 88=15.5%<P>AM/FM stereo cassette: 84=42.6% 85=42.6% 86=46.8% 87=44.0% 88=68.3%<P>AM/FM stereo cass w/eq: 84=0.0% 85=23.4% 86=28.0% 87=16.7% 88=15.4%<P><B>1988 Breakdown by color and body style</B><BR> <BR>(BR)Bright Red: 5665 coupes + 1966 Formulas + 2607 GTs = 10238 <BR>(W)White: 3576 coupes + 1303 Formulas + 1525 GTs = 6404 <BR>(BK)Black: 2072 coupes + 1106 Formulas + 1424 GTs = 4602 <BR>(RR)Ruby Red: 1368 coupes + 567 Formuas + 794 GTs = 2729 <BR>(S)Silver: 738 coupes + 261 Formulas + 257 GTs = 1256 <BR>(Y)Yellow: 489 coupes + 436 Formulas + 241 GTs = 1166 <P><B>1988 Breakdown by option</B><BR> <BR>T-Top: 339 coupes + 299 Formulas + 614 GTs = 1252 <BR>Leather interior: 1324 <BR>5 Speed: 2550 <P>-------------------------------------------<P><BR>I hope this helps... <BR>-Haze   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/84indyfierosig.jpg">      ---      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RedandSilveratFierorama.jpg">     ---      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole_6.gif">    <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 09-18-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||FieroJoe||09-17-2001||08:30 AM||||Very cool!  A great one for the archives!||||reg||1
Z||000002||NEPTUNE||09-17-2001||04:55 PM||||When was the 2M6 made?<BR>What mekes a 2M6 different from an SE?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Steve Normington||09-17-2001||05:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by NEPTUNE:<BR><B>When was the 2M6 made?<BR>What mekes a 2M6 different from an SE?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>2M6 was never a model designation, it was just an additional set of numbers/letters (Like 2.8 MFI on the bumper of 80's Camaros). The 6 cylinders were made from 85-88 but I think Pontiac stopped labeling them 2M6 in 86.<P>PS. 2M6 means 2 seater, Mid-engined, 6 cylinder.||||reg||1
